trategic move here.\n\n\n", 'output': "Evaluation: The board shows [Ac, Ad, 6c, 4d]. With [9c, Qd], my best hand is a Pair of Aces with a Queen kicker (A-A-Q-9-6). The opponent has checked on the Flop and Turn, indicating weakness, but they could be slow-playing an Ace, or hold a pocket pair (6s, 4s, or others) or a King, all of which beat me. Since I am currently leading the overall match and the pot is small, there is no incentive to bloat the pot with a marginal hand. Checking controls the pot size and minimizes variance, allowing me to see the River card for free.\n\nReason: I have a marginal hand (playing the board's pair of Aces with a Q kicker). The opponent's passivity suggests weakness, but betting risks opening myself up to a check-raise or building a pot I cannot win at showdown if they have a King or better pair. Preserving my chip lead by keeping the pot small is the optimal strategy here.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
